{{PlayerIntroduction}}

florescent became the first [[Game Changers]] eligible player to compete in a [[VCT]] International League, joining [[Apeks]] in VCT EMEA for the VCT 2025 season.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://x.com/apeksgg/status/1864715104786485621|title=Her Flor is your Apeks - Welcome @florscnt to @ApeksValorant|date=2024-12-05|author='''[[Apeks]]'''}}</ref> With Apeks, florescent competed in VCT 2025's [[VCT/2025/EMEA_League/Kickoff|EMEA Kickoff]] and [[VCT/2025/EMEA_League/Stage_1|EMEA Stage 1]] before announcing a step back from competing for the rest of 2025 citing personal and family emergencies, as well as finding the relocation to Berlin, where VCT EMEA is located, extremely challenging. florescent remained under contract with [[Apeks]], but would be allowed to explore options if choosing to return in 2025. <ref name="Apeks inactive">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/apeksgg/status/1916914654481179080|title=Update from Apeks|date=2025-04-28|author=[[Apeks]]}}</ref><ref name="flor inactive">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/florscnt/status/1916916260295541146|title=I’m going to be taking off the rest of the 2025 VCT season to rest up and recharge. I may return to competing again in the future but that isn’t something I’m putting much thought into right now.|author='''florescent'''|date=2025-04-28}}</ref>

On May 18<sup>th</sup> 2025, [[Riot Games]] announced they were launching an investigation into sexual-assault allegations raised against an unnamed competitor, understood to be florescent. Riot Games stated that they were investigating whether these allegations would impact the player's future eligibility in ''VALORANT'' and that they would cooperate with any legal investigation.<ref name="Riot Investigation">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/ValorantEsports/status/1924200821660528777|title=An update regarding recently raised allegations|author=[[Riot Games]]|date=2025-05-18}}</ref>  florescent denied any allegations of sexual-assault and sought legal advice in response to the allegations.<ref name="flor response">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/florscnt/status/1923797866344075396|title=I'm aware of the allegations...|author='''florescent'''|date=2025-05-17}}</ref>

On March 30<sup>th</sup> 2026, Riot Games named florescent as the subject of this investigation alongside announcing its conclusion. Their update found there was not sufficient evidence to determine any violation of their Code of Conduct. No penalties were issued and florescent remains eligible to compete in Riot-sanctioned events.<ref name="Procedural Update">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/valesportsna/status/2038693548476993554|title=Procedural Update: Ava “florescent” Eugene|author=[[Riot Games]]|date=2026-03-30}}</ref>
